<p>Colombian President Gustavo Petro visited Caracas on April 24 for talks with Venezuela&#x27;s acting president, Delcy Rodríguez. He became the first foreign leader to travel to Venezuela since Nicolás Maduro was ousted earlier this year. The two governments said they would deepen military cooperation against criminal groups and &quot;mafias&quot; operating along their shared border, making security the clear focus of the meeting. The visit matters because Colombia and Venezuela share a long, porous frontier that has long been affected by smuggling, armed groups and weak state control. It also came after the extraordinary events described by Le Monde and Al Jazeera surrounding Maduro&#x27;s capture in Caracas on January 3; Le Monde reported that he was taken to New York to face drug trafficking charges.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/GHtS6A3Op4ePDzXFCQJe84BQ-KVmUpAqX4sHt7o8_XNdRf4kbXU3wmSTf8z4rweRipqUXTST9vlMgRI7l1eo6nXk9ug3pXK-G0zR8VEivCIc47k3mltkN0EODs6XAwLycm2fY2oWsYvKc8G_fFsYEJnUqMogqEPhWRWzsvb4hjHZfUDqm0kDx_GBteToWeedQ8xaRzRV52YRGVAjE7by489FemIRo2ZBpGN7ZrpH5CGrwOe2oN2i8Zw' alt='Colombian President Gustavo Petro, left, and Venezuela&#x27;s acting President Delcy Rodriguez shake hands after a meeting at Miraflores Palace in Caracas, Venezuela, on April 24, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Border focus: Al Jazeera said border security was expected to dominate the talks, highlighting how urgently both governments view cross-border crime and instability.</li><li>First outreach: Petro&#x27;s arrival marked the first visit by a foreign president to Venezuela since Maduro&#x27;s ouster, giving the meeting symbolic weight beyond the security agenda.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Colombian government: Petro used the visit to push for closer coordination along the shared border, with military cooperation against criminal groups framed as a practical priority. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/colombia-venezuela-hold-key-talks-in-post-maduro-visit/a-76930133'>DW</a>)</li><li>Venezuelan authorities: Rodríguez welcomed Petro at Miraflores presidential palace, signaling that the acting government wants early diplomatic engagement and a working relationship with neighboring Colombia. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/colombias-leader-visits-venezuela-key-talks-acting-president-132361599'>ABC News</a>)</li><li>Regional media framing: Coverage emphasized that the meeting was shaped by the post-Maduro transition, with security cooperation seen as the most immediate area where both governments can show results. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/24/petro-becomes-first-president-to-visit-venezuela-since-maduro-abduction'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/colombia-venezuela-hold-key-talks-in-post-maduro-visit/a-76930133'>Colombia, Venezuela hold  key talks in post-Maduro visit</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/25/venezuela-colombia-pledge-military-cooperation-on-first-post-maduro-visit_6752811_4.html'>Venezuela, Colombia pledge military cooperation on first post-Maduro visit</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/24/petro-becomes-first-president-to-visit-venezuela-since-maduro-abduction'>Petro becomes first president to visit Venezuela since Maduro abduction</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/colombias-leader-visits-venezuela-key-talks-acting-president-132361599'>Colombian leader visits Venezuela for key talks with acting President Delcy Rodríguez</a> - abcnews.com</li></ul>